Paninda revision 013 — stock receiving and Management spacing
Date: 2026-11-06 (Asia/Manila)
Branch: litmus_4
Base: cc26d4a

REQUEST
Implement Stock Receiving under Management and make gaps between Vendors,
Stock Counts and Stock Alerts consistent. Preserve the existing local-first,
modular adapter, clean-data and no-migration testing requirements.

IMPLEMENTED
- Tools Management now groups Vendors, Stock Receiving, Stock Counts and Stock
  Alerts with Arrangement.spacedBy(8.dp). Section breaks remain 24dp.
- Separate receiving history, new-entry, details and picker Kotlin files with
  page-specific string resources. History searches vendor/reference/recorder and
  filters received dates; fixed headers/search and isolated lists/FAB padding.
- New delivery: choose active vendor; select that vendor's active products,
  including zero-stock products; enter quantities, received date and recorder,
  optional delivery reference/notes. Changing vendor confirms clearing lines.
  Drafts survive recreation, leaving warns before discard, confirmation explains
  additive stock and avoiding duplicate deliveries. Editor hides bottom navigation.
- Separate StockDelivery/StockDeliveryItem domain models and ReceivingRepository.
  Atomic save writes immutable vendor/product/SKU snapshots, positive RECEIVING
  movements, product versions/timestamps and pending changes. Stable record IDs
  make repeat saves idempotent. No selling-price or payment change.
- Reject empty/duplicate lines, quantities outside 1..1,000,000, inactive/mismatched
  vendor/products, invalid/future dates and stock/version overflow before writes.
  Received date maps to midnight Asia/Manila; actual recording time is retained.
  Backdated entries affect current stock on save without rebuilding past counts.
- Room delivery tables/DAO/state, reset and transactional sync import/export now
  include delivery history. Existing stock reports observe receiving movements;
  product details label receiving correctly. Notification recovery/rearming follows
  the same committed stock data. Counts opened before delivery reject stale stock.
- Sheets adds StockDeliveries and StockDeliveryItems (Paninda), making ten app
  worksheets with A1 headers. Validates historical snapshots, references, distinct
  lines and exact receiving movement source/quantity/date matches. Names/current
  assignments can change later without rewriting delivery snapshots.
- Fresh Room/schema metadata remain version 1 with revised exported schema. No
  migrations, schema upgrades or backward compatibility. Use uninstall/new file
  or fresh app worksheets for testing. Setup text and contract now say ten pages.
- Updated prototype, workbook/setup/notification docs and Mermaid DFD sources;
  Level 1 adds process 7.0 Receive Stock Deliveries, keeping existing numbers.

VERIFICATION
Two focused receiving checks cover
atomic validation/idempotency/overflow/stale counts, snapshot retention,
Sheets validation and reset/import. Existing UI smoke adds receiving creation
and recreation. Notification check now uses a real receiving save to prove
restocking recovery. No maintained layout tests or demo data added.

LIMITS
No purchase orders, cost accounting, vendor payments, returns, editing/voiding
posted deliveries or automatic sync. Inventory/vendor/product receiving shortcuts
outside Management are not added in this request. Live device/Google acceptance
remains documented separately. No GitHub push or Drive upload requested.

FINAL CHECKS
- All 30 maintained checks passed. After the final editor error-scroll refinement,
  the existing end-to-end UI smoke passed again.
- Two ignored, temporary renders inspected: Management cards have equal 8dp gaps;
  receiving form uses the existing palette, item cards and icon action button.
  No screenshot/layout tests were added to maintained sources.
- assembleDebug and lintDebug passed; lint reports zero errors/fatal findings
  and 28 warnings. git diff --check passed.
- APK: app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk (local build only).
- No physical-device or live Google round-trip acceptance claimed. Fresh install
  and fresh ten-worksheet app contract required; no migration added.
